{"id": "clm:381f9dc912624a4aff9372313bfd45597ef1245858ae4db5829b8f5874323bb6", "type": "statement", "text": "Validate certificate details and trust before deployment, retain previous files for rollback, and test a fresh connection after replacement. An established session alone does not demonstrate successful use of renewed material. Inspect rotation logs as part of validation. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/", "https://docs.itential.com/itential-platform/administer/mongodb"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:155eb55877da47fa6d5824ce07e954c0e74bb978266d8e0915be53be33669ef9", "ev:6e9670fbb0327d21a5aeabecc173bcb89df69429a4d7f23a6fb4eb4ddc6c2aa5", "ev:bc578b93bed0cd4d5562daf163c5148d66252891f59d1bf64ec3b74ce68ff458"]}
{"id": "clm:1bd2d486597334e6fcdd4fb049b2529cf84297f97d5753ff35ed074a16085d68", "type": "statement", "text": "For MongoDB 8.0, replace configured PEM files, then run db.adminCommand({rotateCertificates: 1}) against each target mongod or mongos. The command was introduced in 5.0; db.rotateCertificates() wraps it. Rotation is process-local and can run regardless of replication status. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/", "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-net-tls-secure-connections/view", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a900bdf646ff975ec35fc16587f84c7a292aae48e9fc2bf89ba0c06d5b290309", "ev:af40448a02567d7a017f1a0c8f35ef793c014dca90a954f75d8164a8fd5daf23"]}
{"id": "clm:e9c52a1f7cba521d2f1e29bf0a0a5261d0b18e578f2d6132104aa4fd887dcf11", "type": "statement", "text": "Incorrect, expired, revoked or missing certificate files cause rotation to fail without invalidating the loaded TLS configuration or terminating mongod or mongos. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/rotateCertificates.md", "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0263723f3a2711d606eaa7fbefae6dd4e138bf986951ebf55d571736d1b09268"]}
{"id": "clm:f63028dc36aa4bd31ba6bf5e0935771931f98518dff74c176b1d0d3497b2a99e", "type": "statement", "text": "Only one rotation may run per process, regardless of replication status. A concurrent rotation errors; tlsCertificateSelector=thumbprint also fails rotation and logs a warning. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/rotateCertificates.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4f0ffd631cb7d0b715da2251ddf80084d256a982eea57f995f3e68d072988547", "ev:5da047cfcbe8e4e8efe5fa2816c4d27a7e4a2954bbb83d4e2b4ecffff19f6335"]}
{"id": "clm:7b3937aed1c8ecd5dbd52c637458d917529d340379de004366ae522e0ecd2570", "type": "statement", "text": "Percona's August 31, 2026 procedure explicitly covers same-CA renewal with unchanged X.509 membership attributes. It excludes changing the issuing CA or subject identity from that procedure; this restriction does not mean MongoDB cannot reload a CA file. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-08-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4dd1be1d327e06dea6f1400a8538bbd28a03a8d407576f9e70f863f90dfef6c7", "ev:c5f79abb7f3bda055dfaafffe6a87cca2c835a1478a892e49fb0013d79ea1ddb"]}
{"id": "clm:d9bb38f75bdcb613a9dd440e8a381e3dfe760e3cd9e453644c58d88bed193378", "type": "statement", "text": "Replacement files must retain their configured filenames and paths. Encrypted certificateKeyFile replacements must retain the configured password; interactive password prompting is unsupported. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:98a432de9b3898bc1e898b2935a6c95b8f3b01ba93c9ef4091fdffc95f766998"]}
{"id": "clm:6a75443f4f54c5340b2c116686f425991a197ca9e135e2624e7fcce97654d30a", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 8.0 supports reloading TLS certificates, CA files and CRL files; CRL rotation is documented for Linux and Windows. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/rotateCertificates.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:60f258839727edf9ed88fb47f19dccfce25cebd487aea78803b59498bf1a2321", "ev:c5f79abb7f3bda055dfaafffe6a87cca2c835a1478a892e49fb0013d79ea1ddb"]}
{"id": "clm:01742bc2716f86c865ac5ea6a61bd1aeaa1fd567b15064f2f2f41cf4cef43387", "type": "statement", "text": "Successful rotation preserves established connections using their old certificates; subsequent connections use the newly loaded certificates. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/", "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bc578b93bed0cd4d5562daf163c5148d66252891f59d1bf64ec3b74ce68ff458"]}
{"id": "clm:0784b6a02bb1c7c57b1e3a817aff5fe66ea75175f3475a63bbb3095085554aba", "type": "statement", "text": "The rotateCertificates privilege is required and is included in hostManager. Successful rotation logs certificate identity, thumbprint and validity information; enabled auditing also records it. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:af5f991cee04c236297ec239ddd07fa82fd70b7b86888db6a6f6f75ffc8b3e8b"]}
{"id": "clm:fcb6a21c9fe46856f7a146bee8366e636bfe26baacf5e67d7fe9ba080fc02dae", "type": "statement", "text": "Itential's MongoDB administration procedure replaces server and CA files and uses secondary-first rolling restarts with primary stepdown. That application-specific procedure does not establish that MongoDB 8.0 requires restarts for an eligible online reload. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)", "source_url": "https://docs.itential.com/itential-platform/administer/mongodb", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:098f505ce651dd93a1b792f20c2703eccb229f7fa5a7101cb4318bf98dc18633", "ev:79202e708d7680a8df7ff817b59cae4ae48b1f04e2433930301d1098adabc0e1", "ev:b021279b9e4e6fc96b66029a9f911b363b4819bd22ba1a54c8250287ce2e7785"]}
